From 7ff64f0b56ef5bfae15c6010c10636d6dae2ca0c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:10:41 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(desktop): chat WebSocket connect limit follows slow-link
 mode (15 s -> up to 60 s) [daveey]

Over a slow link the chat WebSocket still gave up after a fixed 15 s, so chat
showed "Reconnecting to Hermes" while slow-link mode (#1928,
apps/desktop/electron/slow-link.ts) kept the HTTP side of the same SSH tunnel
alive.

- shared JsonRpcGatewayClient.connect(wsUrl, { connectTimeoutMs }) takes a
  per-dial limit (the constructor default stays 15 s); a dial that hits its
  limit rejects with code GATEWAY_CONNECT_TIMEOUT.
- Desktop main (slow-link.ts): RemoteTransports maps an SSH-forwarded
  backend's origin to its scope and SSH-master check (registered by
  noteRemoteConnect). gatewayConnectLimitMs(wsUrl) = 15 s, or
  SlowLinkTracker.scaleTimeout(15 s) (x4, capped 60 s) while that link is slow.
  A socket that opened is an answer for the tracker; a dial that timed out
  with the SSH master alive is a strike, like a dispatch-probe timeout.
  Exposed as hermes:gateway:connect-limit (sync) and
  hermes:gateway:connect-outcome via preload; registered with
  registerGatewayConnectIpc. main.ts is net 0 lines.
- Renderer: HermesGateway.connect dials through dialWithLinkLimit
  (src/api/gateway-link-dial.ts), which reads the limit before the dial and
  reports the outcome. No bridge, or a non-positive answer, = client default.
- Local and cloud backends (any URL main does not know as SSH-forwarded) keep
  15 s.

Known cost: when WebSocket strikes alone reach SLOW_LINK_STRIKE_LIMIT, the link
leaves slow mode (logged "giving up on slow mode"); retiring the backend stays
with the dispatch probe, which runs again before the renderer's next dial.

Tests (executed, fake timers):
- src/api/gateway-link-dial-slow-link.test.ts drives the real tracker, the
  main-side limit/outcome functions, dialWithLinkLimit and the shared client
  against a socket that opens at 20 s: it connects in slow mode (60 s limit)
  and times out at 15 s in normal mode and for a local backend; a timeout with
  the master alive enters slow mode, a dead master does not; an open clears
  strikes; IPC registration answers the sync limit.
- src/api/gateway-link-dial.test.ts: HermesGateway.connect passes the limit,
  reports opened / timed-out, ignores other failures, falls back to the default.
- RED: with json-rpc-gateway.ts and client.ts reverted, 11 of the 21 new tests
  fail; GREEN: 21/21.
